      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Major Soil Types in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Indian soils are broadly classified into six major types: Alluvial, Black, Red, Laterite, Desert (Arid), Forest/Mountain soils. Additionally, saline and peat soils occur locally.<img src=\"/books/Precis/Cluster_079_RRB-GK-Geography/images/image_r5h8f6q.jpeg\"/>",
      "id": "82rhao3"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "The fertility of this soil makes the Northern Plains the food bowl of India.",
      "id": "to8fhj5"
    },
    {
